raph><Segment>Click here to add text.</Segment></Paragraph></Element><?property ignore-whitespace="true"?><?property ignore-whitespace="false"?><Element border-color="#000000" editable="true" border-width="0" y="86" name="Text-3" x="357" templateID="" width="243" locked="" bgcolor="" type="Text" padding="0" deletable="" sizePositionLocked="false" height="85" uniqueID="element4"><Paragraph><Segment color="#F99976" font-size="16" font-family="Times New Roman" font-style="bold">PhD-Prehistoric Ceramics</Segment></Paragraph><Paragraph><Segment color="#F99976" font-size="16" font-family="Times New Roman" font-style="bold">MA- Pottery and Sculpture</Segment></Paragraph><Paragraph><Segment color="#F99976" font-size="16" font-family="Times New Roman" font-style="bold">BA - Art History</Segment><Segment>licklick here to add text.</Segment></Paragraph></Element><?property ignore-whitespace="true"?><?property ignore-whitespace="false"?><Element border-color="#000000" editable="true" border-width="0" y="182" name="Text-4" x="173" templateID="" width="671" locked="" bgcolor="" type="Text" padding="0" deletable="" sizePositionLocked="false" height="46" uniqueID="element5"><Paragraph><Segment>Cli</Segment><Segment color="#F974ED" font-size="20" font-family="Times New Roman" font-style="bold">THE RICH HERITAGE OF JAPANESE POTTERY</Segment><Segment>ck here to add text.</Segment></Paragraph></Element><?property ignore-whitespace="true"?><?property ignore-whitespace="false"?><Element border-color="#000000" editable="true" border-width="0" y="261" name="Text-5" x="50" templateID="" width="901" locked="" bgcolor="" type="Text" padding="0" deletable="" sizePositionLocked="false" height="168" uniqueID="element6"><Paragraph><Segment font-size="12" font-style="bold" color="#F99976">Traditional Japanese folk pottery epitomizes work produced with the ease of unconscious thought; it is work that is created without judgment and exemplifies pure artistic energy. Initially, Japanese pottery was produced to hold liquids or grains and to be eaten out of, each form surrendering to caressing hands. The sensation of touch became as important to the potter as that of the visual. </Segment></Paragraph><Paragraph><Segment font-size="12" font-style="bold" color="#F99976"/></Paragraph><Paragraph><Segment font-size="12" font-style="bold" color="#F99976">Ancient Japanese pottery dates back over twelve thousand years to the wondrous ceramics of the Jomon era; it was here that the first coiled pots emerged. Notice the frenetic decorative coils and waving soaring rims that exemplify  this beautiful ancient ware. This Jomon ware of yesteryear is as impetuous and alive as today’s most contemporary work.  </Segment><Segment>lick tT</Segment></Paragraph></Element><?property ignore-whitespace="true"?><Element isImageType="true" sizePositionLocked="false" name="Add an Image-2" link_target="_self" maintainProportion="true" originalSource="" src="Jomon_2000-1000_bc.jpg" height="299" alt="" editable="true" resizeable="true" locked="" deletable="" groupID="30" width="226" WOHratio="0.7569444444444444" y="469" link="" x="79" uniqueID="element7" fileType="IMAGEFILTER" templateID="" type="ImportedImage" zoom="1" offsetY="0" offsetX="0" onPublish="ImportedImage" onPreview="ImportedImage" bucketRatio="0.7569444444444444" imageRatio="0.7569444444444444" rotate="0" brightness="0" contrast="0" colorEffect="" tintRed="0" tintGreen="0" tintBlue="0" borderWidth="0" borderColor="#52A8EC" borderRadius="0" boxShadow="none" glowColor="#52A8EC" origWidth="226" origHeight="299"/><?property ignore-whitespace="false"?><Element sizePositionLocked="false" border-color="#000000" type="Text" uniqueID="element8" deletable="" border-width="0" y="753" x="82" width="177" editable="true" name="Text-6" height="16" padding="0" groupID="30" bgcolor="" locked="" templateID=""><Paragraph><Segment font-style="bold">Jomon 12,500-1,500 bc</Segment></Paragraph></Element><?property ignore-whitespace="true"?><Element is